From bd8961242f2be043c418bcfb58da6599112e6bfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magpie <ccbrian830@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 01:51:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SMC speculative decoding: consolidated core hooks (v0.5.17)

Single-commit consolidation of every live SGLang-side change the external
smcsd package (github.com/abdelfattah-lab/smcsd) needs, re-ported from the
smc_v3-hooks-may2 snapshot (7f36a9bfd, May 2 base) onto v0.5.17 across
3850 upstream commits.  Several of the original 11 hook files were
absorbed or relocated by upstream refactors:

- speculative/spec_info.py: SMC algorithm + SMC_DRAFT/SMC_VERIFY input
  types + SpecInput.use_linear_target_verify() hook.
  get_num_tokens_per_req_for_target_verify returns 1 for SMC draft
  workers: v0.5.17 sizes DecodeCudaGraphRunner buffers via this hook
  (captured_req_width); without it the draft's decode graphs were sized
  for the gamma+1 verify window while capturing 1-token DECODE metadata
  -> illegal memory access at capture (mirrors the DSPARK case).
  supports_spec_v2 hunk dropped (V1 path removed upstream).
- server_args.py + arg_groups/speculative_hook.py: all smc_* knobs as
  declared A[]/Arg fields (CLI auto-generates; ServerArgs is frozen after
  resolution, so SMCEngine's old dynamic-attr pattern is dead -- includes
  smc_power_alpha / smc_defer_bonus / smc_cycle_graph /
  smc_enable_overlap / smc_emit_particle_output).  The SMC validation /
  derived-settings block lives in _handle_smc, dispatched from
  SpeculativeAlgorithm.handle_server_args.  Piecewise CUDA graph
  auto-disable for SMC expressed as a tc_piecewise incompatibility rule.
- model_executor/model_runner.py + runner/base_runner.py:
  _build_dummy_run_spec_info extension point (upstream's
  _decode_cuda_graph_runner_cls supersedes the old _get_graph_runner_class
  hook; kv-pool hooks moved with the alloc_memory_pool refactor).
- runner/decode_cuda_graph_runner.py: SMC draft workers stay out of the
  speculative TARGET_VERIFY capture path (they run their own draft AR
  loop outside this runner).
- mem_cache/unified_memory_pool.py + kv_cache_configurator.py:
  draft_uses_independent_lm -- SMC's draft is a full independent causal
  LM, so it needs a KV slot per full-attention layer, not the single
  layer-0 slot of EAGLE/NextN/MTP heads (was model_runner_kv_cache_mixin,
  deleted upstream).
- configs/model_config.py: gate the draft->MTP architecture rewrite on
  _spec_algo_uses_independent_draft (upstream now carries the
  speculative_algorithm plumbing itself).
- layers/attention/triton_backend.py: SMC linear target-verify metadata
  branch (extend-style causal over a uniform window; the old capture /
  replay graph branches are subsumed by upstream's generalized
  target-verify buffer path) + dispatch to smcsd's split-KV GQA-packed
  verify kernel.  The fast kernel DEFAULTS OFF on this stack pending an
  accuracy investigation: multi-seed GSM8K A/B (Llama-3.1-8B, N=8
  gamma=8, 200q) measured mean 66.7% with it vs 70.0% stock while
  per-call output comparison (~100k calls, SMC_FAST_VERIFY_CHECK=1) found
  no divergence > 5e-2 and synthetic sweeps show only ~4e-3 unbiased bf16
  noise; the gap is p~0.3 -- suggestive, unproven.  Stock costs ~1%
  throughput at short context.  SMC_FAST_VERIFY=1 opts back in;
  SMC_FAST_VERIFY_CHECK=1 keeps the shadow A/B validator
  (SMC_FAST_VERIFY_CHECK_KEEP_FAST=1 to consume fast output while
  logging).
- layers/attention/hybrid_linear_attn_backend.py: monotonic
  init_cuda_graph_state re-init for SMC's shared-backend graph runners,
  extended over v0.5.17's replayssm / mamba-track buffers.
- managers/utils.py: GenerationBatchResult.logprob_diff relay field
  (v0.5.17 _async_d2h idiom).
- compilation/compile.py: piecewise CUDA graph crash fix under python -O
  (carried unchanged).
- pyproject.toml hunk dropped: v0.5.17 already pins kernels>=0.14.1 for
  transformers 5.12.

Validated: smcsd unit suite 47 passed / 1 skipped; GSM8K 10-seed mean
~70% vs old-pin reference 72.0 (same GPU, seed 0: 72.5 new vs 72.0 old)
and doc band 70.2-71.3; 238 tok/s vs 240.

